# Build context for the LM Studio (`llmster`) serving image.
#
# The context is this directory ONLY (see .gitlab/ci/build.yml
# `build-lmstudio` -> DOCKER_CONTEXT), so it is already tiny. This file keeps it
# that way and, more importantly, guarantees that nothing which could carry a
# secret or a model blob is ever sent to the daemon — this image is pushed to a
# registry and embeds a proprietary binary, so context hygiene is not cosmetic.
#
# This is a DENY-ALL allow-list: anything added to this directory is invisible
# to the build until it is named below. `loader/` is un-excluded as a directory
# rather than file by file, because a re-inclusion whose parent is still
# excluded is not reliably honoured.
*
!Dockerfile
!entrypoint.sh
!loader
# ...but never a local node_modules. The image installs the loader's
# dependencies itself with `npm ci` against the committed lockfile; a tree
# built on a developer's machine would carry the wrong platform binaries and
# silently shadow it. (Ordering matters: last match wins, so this must follow
# the `!loader` above.)
loader/node_modules
